    "result_text": "I added the SNAPSHOT audit lines. Three of the four tests pass, but **\"snapshots scenario 3\" still fails**. It fails in the same place with or without my change, so the cause is something else in the app.\n\n**What changed** \u2014 `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/sheet/SaveToday.java`\n- When the sheet's today actually changes, the app now writes `SNAPSHOT sheet=<id> by=<user> name=<name> due-total=<due-total>`, one line per person in list order.\n- The due-totals are taken just before the new date is saved, so they are the figures for the day being left. That puts these lines ahead of any `PERIOD_CLOSED ... auto=yes` lines and the change's ROLLUP/TOTALS lines.\n- Setting today to the date it already has writes nothing.\n- I also updated the header comment in `today.POST.yml` to describe the new lines.\n\n**Test results** (`bin/e2e`)\n- `snapshots`, `snapshots scenario 1` and `snapshots scenario 2` pass. Their expected audit records, including all the SNAPSHOT lines, match.\n- `snapshots scenario 3` fails at `acceptance.spec.ts:926`. After uma changes Ada to grade A from 2026-03-05, the test expects Ada's due-total to be `0.00`, but the screen and the ROLLUP line both show `2.00`.\n- To check whether my change caused it, I put back the original `SaveToday` and ran `bin/e2e` again. Scenario 3 failed at the same line, so I restored my version.\n\n**Why it fails:** before uma's grade change, wes took a statement for Ada while Ada was grade C, which has no rate. That statement recorded her open claim with no figure (\"n/a\"). The test expects that claim to stay n/a once Ada becomes grade A. The code in `statement/TakeStatement.java` only fixes a claim at n/a when its rate had ended; otherwise the claim gets a new figure as soon as a rate applies, so it becomes 2.00. That is a rule about statements, not about the new audit lines. I didn't change it: it's outside this request, and changing it means guessing a business rule that could break other behaviour. If you want scenario 3 to pass, that statement rule needs a separate change, and I can look into it.",
